  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Lines&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Clearly both lines do not have same direction means lines are not parallel.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>Lines are skew lines or intersecting lines.</p><p>Let lines are skew lines and distance between lines is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;if distance between them comes out zero then they will be intersecting lines.</p><p>For lines&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mover><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mover><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math></p><p>Applying here</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>14</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>14</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>Lines are skew lines means do not intersect.</p>",
